  "domain": "infrastructure",
  "definition": "Network Latency is the round-trip communication delay between nodes in a network, directly constraining consensus speed, block propagation, transaction throughput, real-time application responsiveness, and distributed system coordination. High latency increases the probability of forks in blockchain systems, degrades user experience in interactive applications, and sets a fundamental lower bound on achievable synchronisation intervals in geographically distributed deployments.",
